⚡️🇺🇸 The US Department of Energy (DOE) has begun contacting trading firms and refiners to gauge interest in another round of crude loans as part of its 172 Million barrel drawdown from the US Strategic Petroleum Reserve (SPR).

Crude from the Bryan Mound and Big Hill SPR facilities could soon be offered for loading in as early as November/December, with earlier loading dates awarded to those making higher bids. It is not clear what the higher bids would entail, and DOE could choose not to make any awards, as much as 30 Million barrels could be offered.

